    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:b04d5d61d358e759",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "3034b62e46fc5415906b28a92600e1a8f59b4f94e473cf282df6818fe8046710",
      "text": "Breakfast. The Sacred Valley, cradle of the Inca civilisation, was renowned for its fertile land and mild climate, and the Incas built entire towns here, whose ruins remain: Urubamba, with the country estate of the emperor Huayna Cápac; Pisac, said to be shaped like a partridge; Ollantaytambo and its ceremonial centre; Chinchero, with a colonial church built on Inca foundations; and Moray, with its amphitheatre-like agricultural terraces.\n\nNear Pisac, browse the market for silver, ceramics and leather; at the Awanakancha centre, meet llamas, alpacas and vicuñas and learn how their precious wool is dyed. Buffet lunch at a Peruvian restaurant and return to the hotel.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "word_exact",
        "fileId": "1mZ4jhPLYLzUFjyOH1D1pe9UINgA601dT",
        "documentSha256": "698d4b0d33095fd1314e0997e8def9c993a029c02fefffab06a7134a1e5bcd49",
